<blockquote>
<p>But fair enough; I entirely understand your dislike of this one</p>
</blockquote>
<p>I just think that some of the specifics can be altered to allow the Foundation to &quot;naturally&quot; explore this thing than apparently get entrapped by it from the get-go. Putting the station closer to Earth (within the Solar System, but <strong>not</strong> around Earth) should solve the immediate problems- it's close enough to possibly threaten humanity within a relatively short time as well as allowing the Foundation to mount an exploration team.</p>
<p>Heck, although you'll need to rework it a bit, you could incorporate the above into the main narrative- the station (which may have been seen as unremarkable aside from the fact that it's a <em>goddamn space station</em>) suddenly blips from the Solar System to it's orbit around Cygnus. That would certainly be worth sending an exploration team when it becomes clear that the station had undergone some major changes while in transit; probes can only do so much.</p>

